SUBTLE. Spec: the accessors return None when unmeasured. Returning Some(0.0) instead makes
an unmeasured verifier indistinguishable from one measured at zero -- and in the ranking rule
"None sorts below any measured value", a 0.0 sorts equal to a genuinely terrible verifier
rather than being flagged unknown. Requires a test that asserts None specifically.
@@@
    if denominator == 0 {
        return None;
    }
--->
    if denominator == 0 {
        return Some(0.0);
    }
